          "method_draft": "Read the diagram as triangle ABC with segment DE drawn from AB to AC and marked parallel to BC. From the text, AE=12 and EC=18, so E divides AC in the ratio AE:EC = 12:18 = 2:3. By the side-splitter theorem, D divides AB in the same ratio, so AD:DB = 2:3. Since AD=8 corresponds to the 2 parts, one part is 4, so DB=3 parts=12. Then AB=AD+DB=8+12=20.",
